#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-change-review-make.bpmn:18
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Making one requested change to a folio's content on a feature branch: work out its scope, branch, edit the narrative and any deterministic logic, assess what else it touches and how to absorb that, and push. Called from content-change-review once the bean is claimed; it runs on its caller's bean. Revisions after the first push are Task_Iterate in the caller, not a second run of this phase."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-change-review-make.bpmn:112
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "On the edge OUT of `Task_AssessImpact` and before `Task_CommitPush`, because the impact assessment is the evidence the options are weighed against. An analysis before it would compare ways of absorbing a downstream effect nobody has measured yet; one after the commit would be a rationalisation of a choice already pushed. Not between `Task_AssessImpact` and `Task_ReviewImpact`: those are in different processes with no sequence flow between them; the assessment reaches the committee through `Task_CompareBeforeAfter`. In the Agent lane, matching `upstream-version-adoption`: this step produces the options and their trade-offs, and `GW_Approved` in the committee review is where a decision is taken. On the trigger: reaching this call is not the same as running the whole of it. `Process_OptionsAnalysis` opens with `A_Frame`, whose trigger is `opening-brief`'s — irreversibility and surprise, not size — and leaving at that first activity is a correct outcome rather than a skipped step. A copy-edit exits immediately; a logic change that moves an indicator (from `Task_EditLogic`) does not."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-change-review-make.bpmn:111
#. Diagram label
msgid "Options analysis how to absorb the impact"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-change-review-make.bpmn:23
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Owns the technical execution of the change: scoping, branching, editing narrative and deterministic logic, assessing what else it touches, weighing how to absorb that, and pushing. It is also the single re-entry point for the author's and the committee's feedback (Task_Iterate in the caller)."
msgstr ""

